From 691d8e15184d6d7baf40944536dc5980f8b9a685 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_regfile, a multi-port register file as placed
 standard cells
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The net diff of The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD#11669 at its head
691d8e15, all eight commits as one patch: generate_regfile in src/ram,
async_reset, SystemVerilog port headers and `unused <port>`,
write_priority, Port fields named in the spec reader, and RAM-0052 for
what mode netlist leaves unplaced.

generate_regfile builds a register file with many read and write ports
over few words as an array of placed standard cells, from a spec that
names the module, its words and bits, its ports by the RTL's own port
names, and the cells to use. It writes structural Verilog, DEF, an
abstract LEF and a timing model. ORFS's AUTO_MEMORIES_REGFILES (ORFS
patch 0089, The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD-flow-scripts#4651) runs it
during canonicalization.

Upstream as The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD#11669; retires at a bump onto
an OpenROAD that has it.

